      "writtenOn": "2021-05-07T00:24:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In many ways it\u0027d be better to generate build targets for all the versions, to keep the build rule generation static and let the user pick what they want by the target passed to \"m\".\n\nHave you considered that approach? We\u0027d have to add a version list to the sdk modules, but that may be a good thing anyway. I can imagine reasons against it would be ninja rule bloat. Maybe Soong processing time as well, although most of the work ought to be done only once.\n\n+ccross for input on this.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 7,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "defd345f0ebda7b433fd0b8d59a5ac0d0493c5d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "02917803_0619c66f",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 7,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-07T00:24:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Provided we keep the environment variable approach, this has a big impact on the build. Hence I think it\u0027s in order to mention it in the build banner when it\u0027s not the default: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:build/soong/ui/build/dumpvars.go;l\u003d139-165;drc\u003d41ad6b632fb0dae7f9a8c0a9f52125798d811860",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 7,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "defd345f0ebda7b433fd0b8d59a5ac0d0493c5d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c3c79cbb_a7b7f8fe",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 7,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-07T14:28:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The purpose of this environment variable is to avoid having to modify multiple SDKs simply in order to build snapshots for a different version.\n\nThat would be quite tedious, as it would require changes to multiple different repos. They would have to be submitted and allowed to propagate through the branches before the continuous build configuration could be updated at which point developers would have to wait for that to trigger.\n\nUsing the environment variable would simply require updating the continuous build configuration and waiting for it to run.\n\nEach version added would increase the amount of work that the build did for everyone. Cleaning up unused versions would require yet more toil. If versions were branch specific then they would become a source of potential conflict for the sdk modules.",
      "parentUuid": "6fe74b72_8d23433e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 7,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "defd345f0ebda7b433fd0b8d59a5ac0d0493c5d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0ca5822e_b3e8459e",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 7,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-07T14:28:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are no SOONG_ variables present there so I am not sure if adding them there would be the correct thing to do but I think it would be useful.",
      "parentUuid": "02917803_0619c66f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 7,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "defd345f0ebda7b433fd0b8d59a5ac0d0493c5d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1070a4fb_5824db4a",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-07T00:24:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suggest \"unversioned\" for this; it\u0027s more descriptive. Also, following on the subject above, we could consider a mode to disable the SDK snapshot generation altogether to save resources, and \"none\" would be better suited for that.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "defd345f0ebda7b433fd0b8d59a5ac0d0493c5d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aa8f900d_333511d5",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060959
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-07T13:08:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this meant to be used to get modules that override their source equivalent? Meaning `java_sdk_library_import { name: \"framework-sdkextensions\" }` for example?\n\nIsn\u0027t that what current is? Do we need both? (maybe \"current\" should not have a -current suffix?)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "defd345f0ebda7b433fd0b8d59a5ac0d0493c5d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3c6253dd_9c4ba6ab",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-07T14:28:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t see the distinction between ...VERSION\u003dnone and VERSION\u003dunversioned. They mean the same. Sure, \"unversioned\" has more meaning than \"none\" when not used in the context of the snapshot version but that does not happen here.\n\nAlso, using ...VERSION\u003dnone to disable snapshot generation altogether seems a little confusing. If required then an explicit environment variable, e.g. SOONG_SDK_SNAPSHOT_DISABLE\u003dtrue would be clearer.",
      "parentUuid": "1070a4fb_5824db4a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "defd345f0ebda7b433fd0b8d59a5ac0d0493c5d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "68e85c3c_1eef60b3",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-07T14:28:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, they are unversioned modules.\n\n\"current\" (which is the default) creates versioned modules as well as unversioned modules. A versioned module has names of the format \"\u003csdk\u003e_\u003cmodule\u003e@\u003cversion\u003e\". So, \"current\" will create modules called \"\u003csdk\u003e_\u003cmodule\u003e@current\".\n\nAt the moment the \"current\" modules aren\u0027t actually used, although they do help detect and prevent build changes that would break versioned modules.",
      "parentUuid": "aa8f900d_333511d5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "defd345f0ebda7b433fd0b8d59a5ac0d0493c5d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2380f734_3677ebfe",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 18,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060959
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-07T13:08:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we have any way to know what the last frozen sdk snapshot is? For the non-module SDK, we have the prebuilt_sdk module type which looks at all the versions and creates some meta modules like foo-last-frozen based on the contents of the dirs.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 18,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 18,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "defd345f0ebda7b433fd0b8d59a5ac0d0493c5d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5c70ac53_28a1858f",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 18,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-07T14:28:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not yet. Given that we don\u0027t actually have any modules that have been versioned (other then the unused @current) we haven\u0027t needed it. That is a hole that definitely needs fixing.",
      "parentUuid": "2380f734_3677ebfe",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 18,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 18,
        "endChar": 35
      },
